-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:66 ../lsfd-cmd/lsfd.1.adoc:60
-#: ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:76
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*--notruncate*"
-msgstr "*--notruncate*"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:68 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:78
-msgid "Don't truncate output."
-msgstr "Ne pas tronquer la sortie."
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:71
-msgid ""
-"Specify which output columns to print. The default list of columns may be "
-"extended if _list_ is specified in the format _+list_."
-msgstr ""
-"Spécifier quelles colonnes de sortie afficher. La liste des colonnes par "
-"défaut peut être étendue si la _liste_ est spécifiée sous la forme _+list_."
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:74
-msgid ""
-"Output all available columns. *--help* to get a list of all supported "
-"columns."
-msgstr ""
-"Afficher toutes les colonnes disponibles. Utilisez *--help* pour obtenir une "
-"liste de toutes les colonnes disponibles."
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:75
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*-p*, *--pwd*"
-msgstr "*-p*, *--pwd*"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:77
-msgid "Display information related to login by password (see also *-afL*)."
-msgstr ""
-"Afficher les informations relatives à la connexion par mot de passe (voir "
-"aussi *-afL*)."
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:80 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:87
-msgid "Raw output (no columnation)."
-msgstr "Sortie brut (pas de colonnes)."
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:81
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*-s*, *--system-accs*"
-msgstr "*-s*, *--system-accs*"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:83
-msgid ""
-"Show system accounts. These are by default all accounts with a UID between "
-"101 and 999 (inclusive), with the exception of either nobody or nfsnobody "
-"(UID 65534). This hardcoded default may be overwritten by parameters "
-"*SYS_UID_MIN* and *SYS_UID_MAX* in the file _/etc/login.defs_."
-msgstr ""
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:84 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:91
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*--time-format* _type_"
-msgstr "*--time-format* _type_"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:86 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:93
-msgid ""
-"Display dates in short, full or iso format. The default is short, this time "
-"format is designed to be space efficient and human readable."
-msgstr ""
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:87
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*-u*, *--user-accs*"
-msgstr "*-u*, *--user-accs*"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:89
-msgid ""
-"Show user accounts. These are by default all accounts with UID above 1000 "
-"(inclusive), with the exception of either nobody or nfsnobody (UID 65534). "
-"This hardcoded default maybe overwritten by parameters UID_MIN and UID_MAX "
-"in the file _/etc/login.defs_."
-msgstr ""
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:92
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*--wtmp-file* _path_"
-msgstr "*--wtmp-file* _chemin_"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:94
-msgid "Alternate path for wtmp."
-msgstr "Autre chemin pour wtmp."
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:95
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*--lastlog* _path_"
-msgstr "*--lastlog* _chemin_"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:97
-msgid "Alternate path for *lastlog*(8)."
-msgstr "Autre chemin pour *lastlog*(8)."
-
-#. type: Labeled list
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:98 ../misc-utils/findmnt.8.adoc:208
-#: ../misc-utils/lsblk.8.adoc:175 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:97
-#, no-wrap
-msgid "*-y*, *--shell*"
-msgstr "*-y*, *--shell*"
-
-#. type: Plain text
-#: ../login-utils/lslogins.1.adoc:100 ../sys-utils/lsipc.1.adoc:99
-msgid ""
-"The column name will be modified to contain only characters allowed for "
-"shell variable identifiers. This is usable, for example, with *--export*. "
-"Note that this feature has been automatically enabled for *--export* in "
-"version 2.37, but due to compatibility issues, now it's necessary to request "
-"this behavior by *--shell*."
-msgstr ""
-"Le nom de la colonne sera modifié pour ne contenir que des caractères "
-"autorisés dans les variables de l'interpréteur de commande. Ceci est "
-"utilisable, par exemple, avec *--export*. Notez que cette fonctionnalité a "
-"été automatiquement activée pour *--export* dans la version 2.37 mais, à "
-"cause de problèmes de compatibilités, il est maintenant nécessaire de "
-"demander ce comportement avec *--shell*."
-
-#. type: Labeled list
